{"name":"Watermelon Sugar","hex":"#e42b73","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"watermelon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the species Citrullus lanatus, bearing a melon-like fruit.","The fruit of the watermelon plant, having a green rind and watery flesh that is typically bright red when ripe and contains black seeds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/watermelon"},{"term":"sugar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food consisting of small, sweet crystals, principally of sucrose, obtained from sugar cane or sugar beet and used as sweetener and preservative.","Any specific variety of sugar."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add sugar to; to sweeten with sugar.","To make (something unpleasant) seem less so."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sugar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Watermelon Sugar","blocks":[{"text":"\"Watermelon Sugar\" is a song by English singer-songwriter Harry Styles from his second studio album, Fine Line (2019), included as the album's second track. Styles wrote the song with Mitch Rowland and the song's producers, Tyler Johnson and Kid Harpoon. They were inspired by the American novel In Watermelon Sugar (1968) by Richard Brautigan. \"Watermelon Sugar\" is a horn and guitar-driven funk-pop, pop rock song."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bf/Watermelon_Sugar_-_Harry_Styles.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watermelon_Sugar"},{"title":"Watermelon","blocks":[{"text":"The watermelon is a species of flowering plant in the family Cucurbitaceae. It is a scrambling and trailing vine-like plant cultivated worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Taiwan_2009_Tainan_City_Organic_Farm_Watermelon_FRD_7962.jpg/330px-Taiwan_2009_Tainan_City_Organic_Farm_Watermelon_FRD_7962.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watermelon"},{"title":"Sugar","blocks":[{"text":"Sugar is a class of sweet-tasting, soluble carbohydrates, many of which are used in food. Simple sugars, also called monosaccharides, include glucose, fructose and galactose. Compound sugars, also called disaccharides or double sugars, are molecules made of two bonded monosaccharides; common examples are sucrose, lactose and maltose. White sugar is almost pure sucrose. During digestion, compound sugars are hydrolysed into simple sugars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg/330px-Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sugar"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9f/Harry_Styles_Watermelon_Sugar_Music_Video_Still.png/330px-Harry_Styles_Watermelon_Sugar_Music_Video_Still.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9f/Harry_Styles_Watermelon_Sugar_Music_Video_Still.png/330px-Harry_Styles_Watermelon_Sugar_Music_Video_Still.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Styles posing with models to take a picture. This was compared to the ending of Styles's \"Kiwi\" video.[64]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarry_Styles_Watermelon_Sugar_Music_Video_Still.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Watermelon_cross_BNC.jpg/500px-Watermelon_cross_BNC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Watermelon_cross_BNC.jpg/1280px-Watermelon_cross_BNC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Watermelon_cross_BN